for top quality security services for a premium of under $4k per annum making
the extraordinarily pessimistic assumption that you will need one security
officer for every 20 people (ignoring, by the way, the costs of the private
security guards that I already pay for -- I'm just considering the "police"
replacements and their lawyers,e tc). This is, by the way, purely off the
cuff -- don't hold me to it. At the same time, there is one other service
that I get "for free", specifically roadways. I would hazard a guess that
$2000 a year would manage to pay for the roadways I personally use. This
would add up, very very generously, to $6k/year. (I suspect that the true
figures are much lower, but I'm putting upper bounds here). At the same time,
